0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#start-here-a-cas-process-is-not-stateless","title":"Start here: a CAS process is not stateless"},{"depth":2,"url":"#scale-vertically-first-by-composing","title":"Scale vertically first, by composing"},{"depth":2,"url":"#eviction-is-your-capacity-control-and-its-default-thrashes","title":"Eviction is your capacity control, and its default thrashes"},{"depth":3,"url":"#size-the-ac-and-the-cas-together","title":"Size the AC and the CAS together"},{"depth":2,"url":"#sharding-and-what-changing-it-costs","title":"Sharding, and what changing it costs"},{"depth":2,"url":"#going-horizontal","title":"Going horizontal"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-ceilings-you-hit-before-you-expect-to","title":"The ceilings you hit before you expect to"},{"depth":2,"url":"#metrics-nothing-is-on-by-default","title":"Metrics: nothing is on by default"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-the-repository-actually-ships","title":"What the repository actually ships"},{"depth":2,"url":"#when-it-doesnt-work","title":"When it doesn't work"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Scaling the CAS"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"How to grow the content-addressable store: composing tiers, sizing eviction, sharding, and the specific reasons a second CAS replica is harder than a second worker."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," you run a CAS that real builds depend on, and it is\nrunning out of disk, running out of throughput, or both. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at\nthe end:"}]," a store composition sized for your load, an eviction policy that\ndoesn't thrash, and a clear-eyed view of what running more than one CAS process\ncosts. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," an afternoon to size and tune; longer if you go horizontal."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"A CAS that real builds depend on."}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/operate/scaling-workers","children":"Scaling workers"}]," is the straightforward half of capacity. This\nis the other half, and it is a different problem: a worker holds nothing, so\nadding one is free. The CAS holds everything, so adding one is a design\ndecision."]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"start-here-a-cas-process-is-not-stateless","children":"Start here: a CAS process is not stateless"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Most guidance about scaling services assumes replicas are interchangeable. For\nForge's CAS that assumption is wrong in five specific places, and every\nhorizontal-scaling decision on this page follows from them."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"In-flight resumable uploads live in one process."}]," The ByteStream service\nkeeps a registry of active uploads keyed by the upload's UUID, in memory, per\nprocess."]}],"\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-service/src/bytestream_server.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-service/src/bytestream_server.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-service/src/bytestream_server.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":["$L8","ByteStreamServer"]}],"\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n