32:["$","p",null,{"children":"Everything above scales one process. If you have exhausted that, here is the\norder to add replicas in."}]
33:["$","ol",null,{"className":"[&>li]:list-none [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-6 my-8 ml-3 border-l-2 border-border pl-10 [counter-reset:step] [&>li]:relative [&>li]:mb-10 [&>li]:last:mb-0 [&>li]:[counter-increment:step] [&>li]:before:absolute [&>li]:before:left-[-57px] [&>li]:before:top-0 [&>li]:before:flex [&>li]:before:h-8 [&>li]:before:w-8 [&>li]:before:items-center [&>li]:before:justify-center [&>li]:before:rounded-full [&>li]:before:border-2 [&>li]:before:border-border [&>li]:before:bg-background [&>li]:before:content-[counter(step)] [&>li]:before:font-mono [&>li]:before:text-sm [&>li]:before:font-semibold [&>li]:before:text-brand [&>li_ul]:my-2 [&>li_ol]:my-2 [&>li_p]:my-2","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Move the backing store off local disk first."}]," Replicas only make sense over\nstorage they can share: S3 or a compatible object store, GCS, Azure, or Redis.\nA filesystem store cannot be shared between processes at all, so this is a\nprerequisite rather than an optimisation. ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/how-to/stores/s3-and-compatible","children":"S3 and\ncompatible"}]," and ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/how-to/stores/redis","children":"Redis"}],"\nare the recipes."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Keep the per-replica fast tier local and private."}]," Each replica gets its own\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," hot tier on its own disk, pointed at the shared slow store. This is\nthe topology that works: shared truth underneath, independent caches above.\nAccept that the hot tiers diverge; they are caches of a cache."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["Remove ",["$","code",null,{"children":"existence_cache"}]," from the replicated path"]}],", or accept that it will\nserve stale positives. No cross-process invalidation exists except for a\nRedis backend with keyspace notifications enabled. If\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"FindMissingBlobs"}]," latency is why you wanted it, a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}]," hot tier gets you\nmost of the same benefit without the correctness hazard."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Make ByteStream uploads sticky."}]," Configure your load balancer for session\naffinity so a client's upload stream and its ",["$","code",null,{"children":"QueryWriteStatus"}]," resume reach the\nsame replica. Without it, every interrupted large upload restarts from zero.\nThis is the single most common way a horizontally scaled CAS gets slower rather\nthan faster."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Set readiness to account for the startup scan."}]," A filesystem store scans its\nentire ",["$","code",null,{"children":"content_path"}]," at boot and builds its index ",["$","em",null,{"children":"before the process binds any\nsocket"}],". During that window there is nothing to connect to: not a degraded\nservice, an absent one. The window grows with the number of files on disk, so\ngive readiness and liveness probes an initial delay that reflects a full cache,\nnot an empty one."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Scale in slowly, and prefer fewer larger replicas."}]," Removing a replica throws\naway a warm fast tier that took hours to fill, and the actions that would have\nhit it now go to the slow store. The CAS is the opposite of the worker pool\nhere: generous, patient, and biased toward vertical growth."]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":["Only then consider ","$L62"]}],", and only if a single shared backend is provably\nthe ceiling. Re-read the cache-flush warning above before you commit to a shard\ncount."]}]}]]}]
34:["$","div",null,{"data-verify-block":"","className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-success/40 bg-success-soft/50 px-5 py-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-foreground","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2.25","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"shrink-0 text-success","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"}]}],"You did it right if"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"[&>p]:my-0 [&>p+p]:mt-2 [&>ul]:my-0","children":["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Store size levels off below ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]," and stays there, rather than sawing up\nto the limit on every write; that saw is ",["$","code",null,{"children":"evict_bytes"}]," being unset."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"A cold build populates the fast tier and the next identical build reads almost\nentirely from it."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Interrupting a large upload and resuming it resumes from where it stopped,\nnot from zero. If it restarts, affinity isn't working."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["An AC hit never resolves to a missing blob. If it does, add\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"completeness_checking"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Restarting a replica does not fail client requests; it fails readiness first,\nand the load balancer takes it out before it stops answering."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Disk usage on each replica's fast tier is bounded and roughly equal."}],"\n"]}]}]]}]
